+---
+- `cargo test -p osq-core --test no_io` fails: `assert_dependencies` expects `["serde", "serde_json"]` and also sees `sha2.workspace`. The key is dotted, so the test's `split_once('=')` returns `sha2.workspace`.
+- Fixing it means editing `crates/core/tests/no_io.rs`, which is a preexisting test outside scope. The task needs `tests.modify: true` and that file in `scope`. The fix is to expect `sha2` and to take the key name before the first `.`.
+- The proposal's verify, `scripts/verify-rust.sh`, cannot pass until then.
